WEBVTT

00:00:11.906 --> 00:00:12.845
How we count approval.

00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:15.751
What is our approval rate?

00:00:16.306 --> 00:00:17.116
It depends how you count.

00:00:17.586 --> 00:00:19.719
Count every try, and this year it reads

00:00:19.804 --> 00:00:20.828
seventy-seven in a hundred.

00:00:21.383 --> 00:00:23.175
Count each order once, and it reads

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:24.156
eighty-six and a half.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.119
Same payments, two answers.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.040
Our rule:

00:00:30.151 --> 00:00:31.601
each order is counted once.

00:00:32.327 --> 00:00:35.057
One order, three tries, approved on the third:

00:00:35.569 --> 00:00:36.849
that is one approved order,

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:37.959
not one in three.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:40.280
A real case:

00:00:40.561 --> 00:00:42.651
one decline reason seemed to jump from

00:00:42.737 --> 00:00:44.913
seven hundred to more than a thousand when

00:00:44.956 --> 00:00:45.681
tries were counted.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.241
Counted by order, it moved from seven

00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:49.777
hundred to under eight hundred.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.541
Two things come out before we count.

00:00:55.053 --> 00:00:57.272
Repeat tries and duplicates fold into

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.062
their order:

00:00:58.082 --> 00:01:00.130
a hundred and forty-nine thousand of them.

00:01:00.472 --> 00:01:01.837
And card-testing attacks,

00:01:02.136 --> 00:01:02.989
which were never customers:

00:01:03.586 --> 00:01:04.866
twenty thousand more tries.

00:01:08.173 --> 00:01:09.367
Then we keep two kinds apart.

00:01:09.794 --> 00:01:10.775
One-time orders:

00:01:11.245 --> 00:01:12.823
ninety-six in a hundred approved.

00:01:13.335 --> 00:01:14.189
Subscription orders:

00:01:14.487 --> 00:01:15.187
eighty-one.

00:01:15.725 --> 00:01:17.687
Mixed together they read eighty-six and a

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.479
half, a number that describes neither.

00:01:22.743 --> 00:01:23.639
And we watch for traps.

00:01:24.364 --> 00:01:25.687
A rate worked out on a list of

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:26.839
failures says nothing.

00:01:27.351 --> 00:01:29.484
Attack traffic left in can cut a rate

00:01:29.612 --> 00:01:30.312
in half.

00:01:30.679 --> 00:01:32.386
And some payments our own record cannot

00:01:32.599 --> 00:01:33.879
see, like phone wallets,

00:01:34.306 --> 00:01:35.714
so they are left out and listed.

00:01:37.932 --> 00:01:38.657
How we count approval:

00:01:39.169 --> 00:01:41.089
each order once, two kinds apart,

00:01:41.388 --> 00:01:44.049
and nothing counted that was never a customer.

